---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Qingdao Cycling Route — Coastline Bike Tour" description="Coastal cycling route from May Fourth Square to Shilaoren Beach. 20km, half day, dedicated bike lanes. Sea views, stops, bike rental tips, and safety info." pageType="Article">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="tag mb-3">Route</p>
      <h1 class="mb-2">Qingdao Coastal Cycling Route</h1>
      <p class="body-lg mb-10 max-w-[65ch]">20km coastal ride from May Fourth Square to Shilaoren Beach. Mostly flat with dedicated bike lanes, sea views the entire way, and plenty of stops for photos, coffee, and beach breaks.</p>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-10">
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Distance</h4><p class="caption">20 km (12.4 miles)</p></div>
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Duration</h4><p class="caption">Half day (3–4 hours)</p></div>
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Difficulty</h4><p class="tag">Easy — mostly flat</p></div>
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Best Time</h4><p class="caption">Spring or autumn, 7–10am</p></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Route overview -->
      <div class="card p-6 mb-10 bg-[var(--color-accent-subtle)]/30">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-3">Route Overview</h2>
        <p class="caption">May Fourth Square → Olympic Sailing Center → Yinhai Marina → Polar Ocean World → Shilaoren Beach. The route follows the coast east from the city center. Dedicated bike lanes cover most of the distance. The road is flat with gentle slopes. Traffic is light east of the Sailing Center. Best ridden counter-clockwise (outbound by sea, return inland).</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Bike rental -->
      <h2 class="h3 mb-4">How to Rent a Bike</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Shared Bikes (Recommended)</h4>
          <div class="caption space-y-2">
            <p><strong>Hello Bike (哈啰单车):</strong> Available via Alipay scan. ¥1.50 per 30 min. Green bikes parked near May Fourth Square and all metro stations.</p>
            <p><strong>Meituan Bike (美团单车):</strong> Also via Alipay or Meituan app. Similar pricing. Yellow bikes.</p>
            <p><strong>How to unlock:</strong> Open Alipay → scan the QR code on the bike → bike unlocks automatically. No deposit needed if you have Alipay credit.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Traditional Rental Shops</h4>
          <div class="caption space-y-2">
            <p><strong>Price:</strong> ¥30–80/day for a decent road or hybrid bike. ¥100–200 for a premium bike.</p>
            <p><strong>Where:</strong> Several shops near May Fourth Square and the Olympic Sailing Center. Look for "自行车租赁" signs.</p>
            <p><strong>What you get:</strong> Helmet, lock, basic repair kit, and a paper map. Bring your passport as deposit.</p>
            <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Shared bikes are more convenient for this route — pick up at May Fourth Square, drop off anywhere near Shilaoren.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Route Stops -->
      <h2 class="h3 mb-6">Route Stops</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 mb-10">
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">1</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">May Fourth Square — Start</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">The modern heart of Qingdao. The red "Wind of May" sculpture is the landmark. Pick up a shared bike from any of the docking stations around the square. The coastal bike lane starts at the east end of the square.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Quick photo stop: 10 min</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">2</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Olympic Sailing Center (5 min east)</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">The 2008 Olympic sailing venue. Marina lined with yachts and waterfront bars. The Qingdao International Sailing Center buildings are architecturally striking. Stop for photos of the boats against the skyline.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Coffee stop:</strong> Several cafes along the waterfront. Try the one near the visitor center — good espresso and sea views.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 15–20 min</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">3</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Yinhai Marina (15 min east)</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">A quieter marina with fishing boats and small cafes. Less touristy than the Sailing Center. Good rest stop with benches and shade. The coastal path here is particularly scenic with rocky headlands and small coves.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 10–15 min</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">4</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Polar Ocean World (10 min east)</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">Optional stop. A large aquarium and marine theme park with polar bears, penguins, and dolphin shows. Good if you have kids or enjoy aquariums. Skip if you are short on time.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Entry:</strong> ¥150–180. Allow 2–3 hours if you go in.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 0 min (pass through) or 2–3 hours (full visit)</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">5</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Shilaoren Beach — The Finish</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">Wide sandy beach with the iconic Old Stone Man (Shilaoren) rock formation offshore. Much less crowded than the city beaches. Perfect for a final rest, a swim, or photos of the rock at sunset. The beach curves south with fine golden sand.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Facilities:</strong> Public toilets, showers (cold water), and a few beachside restaurants. Lock your bike at the racks near the promenade.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 30–60 min</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Safety & Tips -->
      <h2 class="h3 mb-4">Safety & Tips</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Safety</h4>
          <ul class="caption space-y-1">
            <li>Wear a helmet (shared bikes do not come with one — bring your own or rent from a shop)</li>
            <li>Avoid 07:30–09:00 rush hour on the western sections</li>
            <li>Dedicated bike lanes cover most of the route, but watch for pedestrians crossing</li>
            <li>Electric scooters share the bike lane — they are silent and fast</li>
            <li>Carry water; vending machines are sparse on the eastern stretch</li>
            <li>Summer: start by 7am to avoid heat. Winter: not recommended (wind chill)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Route Tips</h4>
          <ul class="caption space-y-1">
            <li>Best months: April–May (cherry blossoms) and September–October (golden light)</li>
            <li>Total elevation gain: less than 50m — very easy</li>
            <li>You can extend to 30km by continuing to Laoshan (add 10km each way)</li>
            <li>Return option: bus 31 or Didi from Shilaoren back to city center</li>
            <li>Shared bikes must be parked in designated zones — check the app for drop-off spots</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <a href="/qingdao-routes/walking" class="btn-outline">Walking Route</a>
        <a href="/qingdao-routes/driving" class="btn-ghost">Driving Route</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
